ete consumer, changing the prior no-consumer decision that removed placeholders.\n\n## Approach\n\nImplement both metrics from Git history in the existing metrics subsystem. Preserve the structured `unavailable` contract when history, Git, or required analyzer data is absent; never fabricate zero or placeholder values. Register, document, and test the metrics through the existing CLI/registry paths.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/metrics/git_metrics.py`\n- metric registry/schema/CLI composition\n- user guide and maintenance runbook\n- focused Git-history fixture tests\n\n## Testing\n\nUse temporary Git histories for growth and cap-change cases, plus shallow/no-Git/unavailable controls.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `module_size_trend` reports Git-derived module-size history with source and confidence metadata.\n- [ ] `cap_change_events` reports Git-derived module-cap changes with source and confidence metadata.\n- [ ] Missing history, unavailable Git, and insufficient evidence produce the existing structured `unavailable` result rather than a zero/placeholder.\n- [ ] Registry, CLI, schema, user guide, and runbook expose the implemented metrics consistently.\n- [ ] Focused Git-history and unavailable-path tests pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/git_metrics.py","reason":"implement Git-derived historical metrics"},{"path":"src/rebar/metrics/registry.py","reason":"register live metric identifiers"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/metrics.py","reason":"surface metrics through existing command composition"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/metrics.schema.json","reason":"preserve structured output contract"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"document implemented metric behavior"},{"path":"docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md","reason":"document Janitor/audit use of metrics"},{"path":"tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics.py","reason":"prove Git-history metric values"},{"path":"tests/unit/metrics/test_git_metrics_heldout.py","reason":"prove unavailable and edge controls"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_metrics_cli.py","reason":"verify CLI/registry exposure"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","metrics","git","rp35"],"ticket_id":"21de-f9d9-475f-414c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Implement Git-backed module-size trend and cap-change metrics","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c6467771-3f60-4f4f-9fe3-fbcd18819e83","f9a78074-ca36-421f-a003-9e88b4f7cfec"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788328054084208001,"uuid":"bde62922-8ee6-4b37-92bf-8880dbda2ca9"}